{"name":"Aubergine Mauve","hex":"#3b2741","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aubergine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Asian plant, Solanum melongena, cultivated for its edible purple, green, or white ovoid fruit; eggplant.","The fruit of this plant, eaten as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aubergine"},{"term":"mauve","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich purple synthetic dye, which faded easily, briefly popular c. 1859‒1873 and now called mauveine.","A pale purple or violet colour, like the colour of the dye after it has faded."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mauve"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eggplant","blocks":[{"text":"Solanum melongena is a plant species in the nightshade family Solanaceae, grown worldwide for its edible fruit, typically used as a vegetable in cooking. It is known by a number of names, including eggplant, aubergine, and brinjal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG/330px-Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant","wikidata":"Q7540"},{"title":"Mauve","blocks":[{"text":"Mauve is a pale purple color named after the mallow flower. The first use of the word mauve as a color was in 1796–1798 according to the Oxford English Dictionary, but its use seems to have been rare before 1859. Another name for the color is mallow, with the first recorded use of mallow as a color name in English in 1611."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Wilde_Malve.JPG/330px-Wilde_Malve.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mauve","wikidata":"Q604079"},{"title":"Eggplant (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Eggplant is a dark purple or brownish-purple color that resembles the color of the outer skin of European eggplants. Another name for the color eggplant is aubergine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Aubergine.jpg/330px-Aubergine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant_(color)","wikidata":"Q1403218"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/500px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/1280px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/500px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg/500px-%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg/1280px-%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg/500px-%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg"},{